import Spaces.LP26.Lemma59
import Spaces.LP26.StandardWA

/-!
# LP26 Corollary 1.2, last clause: `D_{qc,S}(X)` is coherent for `X` Noetherian

Lank–Pauwels, *Gluing weak approximability along recollements* (LP26), **Corollary 1.2**
(`cor:weak_approx_spaces`), last sentence: if `X` is a Noetherian algebraic space and `S ⊆ |X|` is
closed with quasi-compact complement, then `D_{qc,S}(X)` is **coherent** in the sense of LP26 §2
(`sec:prelim_weak_approx`, after Definition 2.1; CHNS, Definition 10.1.1).

## Main definitions and results

* `IsCoherent.{w} C`: LP26's coherence of a triangulated category `C` (coproducts over `Type w`):
  `C` is weakly approximable, and for every `t`-structure `t` in the preferred equivalence class
  there is `N > 0` such that every `Y ∈ 𝒯^-_c` admits a distinguished triangle `X → Y → Z → X[1]`
  with `X ∈ 𝒯^-_c ∩ 𝒯^{≤ N}` and `Z ∈ 𝒯^b_c ∩ 𝒯^{≥ 0}`; `𝒯^-_c`, `𝒯^b_c`, `𝒯^{≤ N}`, `𝒯^{≥ 0}`
  are computed for `t` (`minusC`, `boundedC` of `Spaces/LP26/Lemma59.lean`), the compact objects
  being AxiomMath's `IsCompactObject.{w}` (Stacks 07LS).
* `minusC_eq_of_tStructureEquivalent`, `bounded_eq_of_tStructureEquivalent`,
  `boundedC_eq_of_tStructureEquivalent`: `𝒯^-_c`, `𝒯^b` and `𝒯^b_c` depend only on the
  equivalence class of the `t`-structure (CHNS, Remark 4.1.5, for the class used there).
* `tStructureEquivalent_of_inPreferredClass`: every `t`-structure of the preferred class is
  equivalent to the `t`-structure of any weak approximation data (Neeman, Facts 1.26(i) and
  Remark 2.11; Stacks 09SR is AxiomMath's theorem), and `inPreferredClass_of_paperData`: the
  `t`-structure of weak approximation data is in the preferred class.
* `isCoherent_of_restricts`: **the coherence criterion** (CHNS, Example 10.1.2, as LP26 uses it:
  "a weakly approximable category is coherent if some `t`-structure in the preferred class
  restricts to `𝒯^-_c`"): if `W` are weak approximation data and `𝒯^-_c` (for `W.t`) consists of
  `W.t`-bounded-above objects and is stable under the truncations of `W.t`, then `C` is coherent.
* `inPreferredClass_standardTStructure`: under standard W.A., the standard `t`-structure of
  `D_{qc,T}(X)` is in the preferred class (the first step of LP26's proof of Lemma 5.9,
  `lem:characterize_T-_c`), and `standardMinusC_eq_minusC`: `𝒯^-_c` for any `t`-structure of the
  preferred class is the standard one's, the identification that `Spaces/LP26/Lemma59.lean`
  records as a gap.
* `standardMinusC_truncLE`, `standardMinusC_truncGE`: for `X` Noetherian, the standard
  `t`-structure restricts to `𝒯^-_c = D^-_{coh,T}(X)` (Lemma 5.9).
* `corollary_1_2_coherent`: **Corollary 1.2, last clause**, over algebraic spaces.
* `corollary_1_2_coherent_nonVacuity`: non-vacuity, for the base `S` affine and locally
  Noetherian (for instance `Spec ℤ`).

## Proof

LP26's: by Corollary 1.2 (standard W.A., `corollary_1_2_standard`) there are weak approximation
data on `𝒯 = D_{qc,T}(X)` with the standard `t`-structure; by Lemma 5.9 (Noetherian clauses,
`lemma_5_9_minus_noetherian`) `𝒯^-_c = D^-_{coh,T}(X)` for it, and the standard truncations of an
object of `D^-_{coh,T}(X)` lie in `D^-_{coh,T}(X)` (their cohomology sheaves are those of the
object or zero).  The criterion (CHNS, Example 10.1.2) is proved here: let `t` be in the preferred
class, so `t ∼ t₀ := W.t` (Neeman's equivalence, with constant `N₀ ≥ 0`); `𝒯^-_c` and `𝒯^b_c` are
the same for `t` and `t₀`.  For `Y ∈ 𝒯^-_c` take the `t₀`-truncation triangle
`τ₀^{≤ N₀ - 1} Y → Y → τ₀^{≥ N₀} Y → ⋯`.  Then `τ₀^{≥ N₀} Y ∈ t₀^{≥ N₀} ⊆ t^{≥ 0}` (the coaisles
are the right orthogonals of the aisles, and `t^{≤ -1} ⊆ t₀^{≤ N₀ - 1}`), it is `t₀`-bounded (`Y`
is bounded above) and in `𝒯^-_c` (the restriction), so in `𝒯^b_c`; and
`τ₀^{≤ N₀ - 1} Y ∈ t₀^{≤ N₀ - 1} ⊆ t^{≤ 2 N₀ - 1} ⊆ t^{≤ N}` with `N = 2 N₀ + 1`, and in `𝒯^-_c`.

## Rendering, and how the statement differs from LP26's

* **Coherence** is rendered from LP26's text after Definition 2.1 (which cites CHNS, Definition
  10.1.1).  "The preferred equivalence class" is `SumUniverse.InPreferredClass.{w}` (Neeman,
  Definition 2.9 and Remark 2.11: equivalent to the `t`-structure generated by a compact
  generator), and `𝒯^-_c`, `𝒯^b_c` are computed for the `t`-structure `t` quantified over (they do
  not depend on it within the class, `minusC_eq_of_tStructureEquivalent`).  "Weakly approximable"
  is `SumUniverse.SatisfiesPaperWA.{w}`.  For `D_{qc,T}(X)` the coproduct universe is `w = u`
  (direct sums over `Type u`, AxiomMath's `D(𝒪_X)`), as in `Spaces/LP26/Proposition58.lean`.
* **Hypotheses.**  LP26 states Corollary 1.2 for `X` quasi-compact quasi-separated with
  quasi-finite separated diagonal; the coherence clause adds "Noetherian".  Here `X` is Noetherian
  (AxiomMath's `IsNoetherian`, Stacks 03EA, which includes quasi-compact and quasi-separated) and
  the diagonal hypothesis is not assumed (as `corollary_1_2_standard`); the statement is therefore
  stronger than the paper's.
* As in Lemma 5.9, the instance arguments making `D_qc(X)` and `D_{qc,T}(X)` triangulated are
  instance arguments (`Spaces/Supported/CompactGeneration.lean`).

## Assumptions

The tagged AxiomMath inputs of `corollary_1_2_standard` and of the Noetherian clauses of Lemma 5.9
(`lemma_5_9_minus_noetherian`), and two new ones in `Spaces/LP26/Inputs.lean`:
`CoherentOfIsoInput` (AxiomMath `Stacks.SheafOfModules.isCoherentOnSite_of_iso`) and
`CoherentOfIsZeroInput` (AxiomMath `Stacks.SheafOfModules.isCoherentOnSite_zero`).  Stacks 09SR
is AxiomMath's theorem (`Stacks.tag09SR_paperForm`).  Nothing else.
-/

noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits CategoryTheory.Pretriangulated CategoryTheory.Triangulated
open RelativeWeakApprox RelativeWeakApprox.PaperM2 RelativeWeakApprox.CompactTStructureW6
  RelativeFM.NeemanPreferredM6 RelativeWeakApprox.PaperHypothesesW6

namespace RelativeFM.Spaces.LP26

universe w v u

/-! ### Coherence, and the invariance of `𝒯^-_c` -/

section Single

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] [Preadditive C] [HasZeroObject C] [HasShift C ℤ]
  [∀ n : ℤ, (shiftFunctor C n).Additive] [Pretriangulated C]

variable (C) in
/-- **Coherence** (LP26 §2, `sec:prelim_weak_approx`, after Definition 2.1; CHNS, Definition
10.1.1), for a coproduct universe `w`: `C` is weakly approximable and, for any `t`-structure `t` in
the preferred equivalence class, there is an integer `N > 0` such that every `Y ∈ 𝒯^-_c` admits a
distinguished triangle `X → Y → Z → X[1]` with `X ∈ 𝒯^-_c ∩ 𝒯^{≤ N}` and `Z ∈ 𝒯^b_c ∩ 𝒯^{≥ 0}`
(for `t`, the compact objects being `IsCompactObject.{w}`). -/
def IsCoherent : Prop :=
  SumUniverse.SatisfiesPaperWA.{w} C ∧
    ∀ t : TStructure C, SumUniverse.InPreferredClass.{w} t →
      ∃ N : ℤ, 0 < N ∧ ∀ Y : C, minusC t (fun D => IsCompactObject.{w} D) Y →
        ∃ (X Z : C) (f : X ⟶ Y) (g : Y ⟶ Z) (h : Z ⟶ X⟦(1 : ℤ)⟧),
          Triangle.mk f g h ∈ distTriang C ∧
            minusC t (fun D => IsCompactObject.{w} D) X ∧ t.le N X ∧
            boundedC t (fun D => IsCompactObject.{w} D) Z ∧ t.ge 0 Z

/-- Coaisles from aisles: if `t₂^{≤ k - 1} ⊆ t₁^{≤ k - 1 + N}`, then `t₁^{≥ k + N} ⊆ t₂^{≥ k}`
(the coaisles are the right orthogonals of the aisles, Mathlib's `isGE_iff_orthogonal`). -/
theorem ge_le_ge_of_le_le {t₁ t₂ : TStructure C} {N k : ℤ}
    (h : t₂.le (k - 1) ≤ t₁.le (k - 1 + N)) : t₁.ge (k + N) ≤ t₂.ge k := by
  intro Z hZ
  have : t₁.IsGE Z (k + N) := (t₁.ge_iff_isGE _ _).1 hZ
  rw [t₂.ge_iff_isGE, t₂.isGE_iff_orthogonal (k - 1) k (by omega)]
  intro Y f hY
  have : t₁.IsLE Y (k - 1 + N) := (t₁.le_iff_isLE _ _).1 (h Y ((t₂.le_iff_isLE _ _).2 hY))
  exact t₁.zero f (k - 1 + N) (k + N) (by omega)

/-- `𝒯^-_c` grows along `t₁^{≤ k} ⊆ t₂^{≤ k + N}`. -/
theorem minusC_le_of_le {t₁ t₂ : TStructure C} (P : ObjectProperty C) {N : ℤ} (hN : 0 ≤ N)
    (h : ∀ k : ℤ, t₁.le k ≤ t₂.le (k + N)) : minusC t₁ P ≤ minusC t₂ P := by
  intro E hE n hn
  obtain ⟨D, F, f, g, k, hT, hD, hF⟩ := hE (n + N) (by omega)
  have hF' := h (-(n + N)) F hF
  rw [show -(n + N) + N = -n by ring] at hF'
  exact ⟨D, F, f, g, k, hT, hD, hF'⟩

/-- `𝒯^-` grows along `t₁^{≤ k} ⊆ t₂^{≤ k + N}`. -/
theorem minus_le_of_le {t₁ t₂ : TStructure C} {N : ℤ}
    (h : ∀ k : ℤ, t₁.le k ≤ t₂.le (k + N)) : t₁.minus ≤ t₂.minus := by
  rintro E ⟨n, hn⟩
  exact ⟨n + N, (t₂.le_iff_isLE _ _).1 (h n E ((t₁.le_iff_isLE _ _).2 hn))⟩

/-- `𝒯^+` grows along `t₂^{≤ k} ⊆ t₁^{≤ k + N}`. -/
theorem plus_le_of_le {t₁ t₂ : TStructure C} {N : ℤ}
    (h : ∀ k : ℤ, t₂.le k ≤ t₁.le (k + N)) : t₁.plus ≤ t₂.plus := by
  rintro E ⟨n, hn⟩
  refine ⟨n - N, (t₂.ge_iff_isGE _ _).1 (ge_le_ge_of_le_le (k := n - N) (h (n - N - 1)) E ?_)⟩
  rw [show n - N + N = n by ring]
  exact (t₁.ge_iff_isGE _ _).2 hn

/-- **`𝒯^-_c` depends only on the equivalence class of the `t`-structure** (Neeman's equivalence,
Definition 2.9; CHNS, Remark 4.1.5). -/
theorem minusC_eq_of_tStructureEquivalent {t₁ t₂ : TStructure C} (P : ObjectProperty C)
    (h : TStructureEquivalent t₁ t₂) : minusC t₁ P = minusC t₂ P := by
  obtain ⟨N, hN, hle⟩ := GluedPreferred.exists_le_le_of_tStructureEquivalent h
  exact le_antisymm (minusC_le_of_le P hN fun k => (hle k).1)
    (minusC_le_of_le P hN fun k => (hle k).2)

/-- **`𝒯^b` depends only on the equivalence class of the `t`-structure.** -/
theorem bounded_eq_of_tStructureEquivalent {t₁ t₂ : TStructure C}
    (h : TStructureEquivalent t₁ t₂) : t₁.bounded = t₂.bounded := by
  obtain ⟨N, -, hle⟩ := GluedPreferred.exists_le_le_of_tStructureEquivalent h
  have h₁ : t₁.bounded ≤ t₂.bounded := fun E hE =>
    ⟨plus_le_of_le (fun k => (hle k).2) E hE.1, minus_le_of_le (fun k => (hle k).1) E hE.2⟩
  have h₂ : t₂.bounded ≤ t₁.bounded := fun E hE =>
    ⟨plus_le_of_le (fun k => (hle k).1) E hE.1, minus_le_of_le (fun k => (hle k).2) E hE.2⟩
  exact le_antisymm h₁ h₂

/-- **`𝒯^b_c` depends only on the equivalence class of the `t`-structure.** -/
theorem boundedC_eq_of_tStructureEquivalent {t₁ t₂ : TStructure C} (P : ObjectProperty C)
    (h : TStructureEquivalent t₁ t₂) : boundedC t₁ P = boundedC t₂ P := by
  funext E
  simp only [boundedC, bounded_eq_of_tStructureEquivalent h, minusC_eq_of_tStructureEquivalent P h]

/-- The preferred class is closed under Neeman's equivalence. -/
theorem inPreferredClass_of_tStructureEquivalent {t t' : TStructure C}
    (h : SumUniverse.InPreferredClass.{w} t) (h' : TStructureEquivalent t' t) :
    SumUniverse.InPreferredClass.{w} t' := by
  obtain ⟨G, tG, hGc, hGg, htG, heq⟩ := h
  exact ⟨G, tG, hGc, hGg, htG, tStructureEquivalent_trans h' heq⟩

end Single

/-! ### The preferred class, for a coproduct universe `w` -/

section Preferred

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] [Preadditive C] [HasZeroObject C] [HasShift C ℤ]
  [∀ n : ℤ, (shiftFunctor C n).Additive] [Pretriangulated C] [CategoryTheory.IsTriangulated C]
  [LocallySmall.{w} C] [HasCoproducts.{w} C]

/-- **A `t`-structure of the preferred class is equivalent to the `t`-structure of any weak
approximation data** (Neeman, Facts 1.26(i), Proposition 3.6 and Remark 2.11), for a coproduct
universe `w` independent of the Hom universe.  Proof: in a triangulated model with morphisms in
`Type w` (`SumUniverse.exists_triangulatedEquivalence_of_locallySmall`), both are equivalent to
compactly generated `t`-structures (`tStructureEquivalent_compactlyGenerated`), and two compactly
generated ones are equivalent by Stacks 09SR (AxiomMath's theorem, `Stacks.tag09SR_paperForm`;
`tStructureEquivalent_of_isClassicalGeneratorOnCompacts`); the equivalence is carried back. -/
theorem tStructureEquivalent_of_inPreferredClass
    (W : SumUniverse.PaperWeakApproximationData.{w} C) {t : TStructure C}
    (ht : SumUniverse.InPreferredClass.{w} t) : TStructureEquivalent t W.t := by
  obtain ⟨D', _, _, _, _, _, _, eD, _, _, _, _, _, _, hD'⟩ :=
    SumUniverse.exists_triangulatedEquivalence_of_locallySmall.{w} C
  have := hD' inferInstance
  have : HasCoproducts.{w} D' := SumUniverse.hasCoproducts_of_equivalence eD
  obtain ⟨G, tG, hGc, hGg, htG, heq⟩ :=
    (SumUniverse.inPreferredClass_iff _).1 (SumUniverse.inPreferredClass_transport eD ht)
  let W' := SumUniverse.paperData_equiv (W.transport eD)
  have h₁ := tStructureEquivalent_compactlyGenerated W' _
    (compactTStructure_le_zero W'.G W'.G_compact)
  have h₂ := tStructureEquivalent_of_isClassicalGeneratorOnCompacts _ _ W'.G G
    (compactTStructure_le_zero W'.G W'.G_compact) htG
    (Stacks.tag09SR_paperForm D' _ W'.G_paperGenerates W'.G_compact)
    (Stacks.tag09SR_paperForm D' _ hGg hGc) W'.G_compact hGc
  obtain ⟨n, hn, hle, hge⟩ :=
    tStructureEquivalent_trans heq (tStructureEquivalent_symm (tStructureEquivalent_trans h₁ h₂))
  refine ⟨n, hn, fun X hX => ?_, fun X hX => ?_⟩
  · have := hle (eD.functor.obj X) ((t.le (-n)).prop_of_iso (eD.unitIso.app X) hX)
    exact (W.t.le 0).prop_of_iso (eD.unitIso.app X).symm this
  · have := hge (eD.functor.obj X) ((W.t.le 0).prop_of_iso (eD.unitIso.app X) hX)
    exact (t.le n).prop_of_iso (eD.unitIso.app X).symm this

/-- **The `t`-structure of weak approximation data is in the preferred class** (Neeman,
Facts 1.26(i); BNP, Lemma 3.7), for a coproduct universe `w`: in a triangulated model with
morphisms in `Type w` the transported data give it (`inPreferredClass_of_paperData`), and it is
carried back along the inverse equivalence. -/
theorem inPreferredClass_of_paperData_univ (W : SumUniverse.PaperWeakApproximationData.{w} C) :
    SumUniverse.InPreferredClass.{w} W.t := by
  obtain ⟨D', _, _, _, _, _, _, eD, _, _, _, _, _, _, hD'⟩ :=
    SumUniverse.exists_triangulatedEquivalence_of_locallySmall.{w} C
  have := hD' inferInstance
  have : HasCoproducts.{w} D' := SumUniverse.hasCoproducts_of_equivalence eD
  have h' : SumUniverse.InPreferredClass.{w} (W.transport eD).t :=
    (SumUniverse.inPreferredClass_iff _).2
      (inPreferredClass_of_paperData (SumUniverse.paperData_equiv (W.transport eD)))
  let : eD.symm.functor.CommShift ℤ := inferInstanceAs (eD.inverse.CommShift ℤ)
  let : eD.symm.inverse.CommShift ℤ := inferInstanceAs (eD.functor.CommShift ℤ)
  have : eD.inverse.Additive := eD.toAdjunction.right_adjoint_additive
  have : eD.symm.functor.Additive := inferInstanceAs eD.inverse.Additive
  have : eD.symm.functor.IsTriangulated := inferInstanceAs eD.inverse.IsTriangulated
  have : eD.symm.inverse.IsTriangulated := inferInstanceAs eD.functor.IsTriangulated
  have h'' := SumUniverse.inPreferredClass_transport eD.symm h'
  have heq : SumUniverse.transportTStructure eD.symm (W.transport eD).t = W.t := by
    apply RelativeWeakApprox.TStructure.ext_le_zero
    funext Y
    apply propext
    change W.t.le 0 (eD.inverse.obj (eD.functor.obj Y)) ↔ W.t.le 0 Y
    exact ⟨fun h => (W.t.le 0).prop_of_iso (eD.unitIso.app Y).symm h,
      fun h => (W.t.le 0).prop_of_iso (eD.unitIso.app Y) h⟩
  rwa [heq] at h''

/-- **The coherence criterion** (CHNS, Example 10.1.2, in the form LP26 uses in the proof of
Corollary 1.2: "a weakly approximable category is coherent if some `t`-structure in the preferred
class restricts to `𝒯^-_c`").  Let `W` be weak approximation data with `t`-structure `t₀` such
that, for `t₀`, every object of `𝒯^-_c` is bounded above (`hminus`) and `𝒯^-_c` is stable under
the truncations `τ^{≤ n}`, `τ^{≥ n}` of `t₀` (`hres`: `t₀` restricts to `𝒯^-_c`).  Then `C` is
coherent.  Proof in the module docstring. -/
theorem isCoherent_of_restricts (W : SumUniverse.PaperWeakApproximationData.{w} C)
    {t₀ : TStructure C} (hW : W.t = t₀)
    (hminus : ∀ Y : C, minusC t₀ (fun D => IsCompactObject.{w} D) Y → t₀.minus Y)
    (hres : ∀ Y : C, minusC t₀ (fun D => IsCompactObject.{w} D) Y → ∀ n : ℤ,
      minusC t₀ (fun D => IsCompactObject.{w} D) ((t₀.truncLE n).obj Y) ∧
        minusC t₀ (fun D => IsCompactObject.{w} D) ((t₀.truncGE n).obj Y)) :
    IsCoherent.{w} C := by
  refine ⟨⟨W⟩, fun t ht => ?_⟩
  have hequiv : TStructureEquivalent t t₀ := hW ▸ tStructureEquivalent_of_inPreferredClass W ht
  obtain ⟨N₀, hN₀, hle⟩ := GluedPreferred.exists_le_le_of_tStructureEquivalent hequiv
  have hmC := minusC_eq_of_tStructureEquivalent (fun D => IsCompactObject.{w} D) hequiv
  have hbd := bounded_eq_of_tStructureEquivalent hequiv
  refine ⟨2 * N₀ + 1, by omega, fun Y hY => ?_⟩
  rw [hmC] at hY
  have hT := t₀.triangleLEGE_distinguished (N₀ - 1) N₀ (by omega) Y
  refine ⟨_, _, _, _, _, hT, ?_, ?_, ⟨?_, ?_⟩, ?_⟩
  · rw [hmC]
    exact (hres Y hY (N₀ - 1)).1
  · have h₁ : t₀.le (N₀ - 1) ((t₀.truncLE (N₀ - 1)).obj Y) :=
      (t₀.le_iff_isLE _ _).2 inferInstance
    exact t.le_monotone (show N₀ - 1 + N₀ ≤ 2 * N₀ + 1 by omega) _ ((hle (N₀ - 1)).2 _ h₁)
  · rw [hbd]
    obtain ⟨m, hm⟩ := hminus Y hY
    exact ⟨⟨N₀, inferInstance⟩, ⟨m, inferInstance⟩⟩
  · rw [hmC]
    exact (hres Y hY N₀).2
  · have h₁ : t₀.ge (0 + N₀) ((t₀.truncGE N₀).obj Y) := by
      rw [zero_add]
      exact (t₀.ge_iff_isGE _ _).2 inferInstance
    exact ge_le_ge_of_le_le (k := 0) ((hle (0 - 1)).1) _ h₁

end Preferred

/-! ### Over algebraic spaces -/

open AlgebraicGeometry AlgebraicGeometry.Space

attribute [-instance] Stacks.Cohomology.SiteModules.moduleSheavesAbelian
  Stacks.Cohomology.SiteModules.moduleSheavesGrothendieck

attribute [local instance] HasDerivedCategory.standard smallEtaleRingedSite_hasSheafify
  smallEtaleRingedSite_wEqualsLocallyBijective

attribute [local instance] pointTopology

open Supported

variable {B : BigFppfSite.{u}} {S : Scheme.{u}} {hS : B.Contains S}

section Truncation

variable (X : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS) [(qcohDerived X).IsTriangulated]
  (T : Set (points B S hS X.1))
  [ObjectProperty.IsTriangulated (CohomologySupportedOn B S hS X.1 X.2 T)]

/-- **The standard truncations of `D_{qc,T}(X)` are the canonical ones of `D(𝒪_X)`**: the
underlying objects of `τ^{≤ n} Y` and `τ^{≥ n + 1} Y` (for the standard `t`-structure of
`D_{qc,T}(X)`) are isomorphic to the canonical truncations of `Y` in `D(𝒪_X)` (the image of the
truncation triangle is a distinguished triangle with the same degree bounds, Mathlib's
`TStructure.triangle_iso_exists`). -/
theorem nonempty_iso_truncLE_truncGE (Y : DqcZ X T) (n : ℤ) :
    Nonempty ((((standardTStructure X T).truncLE n).obj Y).obj.obj ≅
        (DerivedCategory.TStructure.t.truncLE n).obj Y.obj.obj) ∧
      Nonempty ((((standardTStructure X T).truncGE (n + 1)).obj Y).obj.obj ≅
        (DerivedCategory.TStructure.t.truncGE (n + 1)).obj Y.obj.obj) := by
  let tO := DerivedCategory.TStructure.t (C := Modules.{u, u} B S hS X.1 X.2)
  have hT := (qcohDerived X).ι.map_distinguished _ ((qcSupportedOn X T).ι.map_distinguished _
    ((standardTStructure X T).triangleLEGE_distinguished n (n + 1) rfl Y))
  obtain ⟨e, -⟩ := tO.triangle_iso_exists hT
    (tO.triangleLEGE_distinguished n (n + 1) rfl Y.obj.obj) (Iso.refl _) n (n + 1)
    (by
      exact (standardTStructure_isLE_iff X T _ n).1
        (show (standardTStructure X T).IsLE (((standardTStructure X T).truncLE n).obj Y) n
          from inferInstance))
    (by
      exact (standardTStructure_isGE_iff X T _ (n + 1)).1
        (show (standardTStructure X T).IsGE
          (((standardTStructure X T).truncGE (n + 1)).obj Y) (n + 1) from inferInstance))
    (by change tO.IsLE ((tO.truncLE n).obj Y.obj.obj) n; infer_instance)
    (by change tO.IsGE ((tO.truncGE (n + 1)).obj Y.obj.obj) (n + 1); infer_instance)
  exact ⟨⟨Triangle.π₁.mapIso e⟩, ⟨Triangle.π₃.mapIso e⟩⟩

/-- **The standard truncations preserve coherent cohomology**: if every `Hⁱ(Y)` is coherent, so
is every `Hⁱ(τ^{≤ n} Y)` and every `Hⁱ(τ^{≥ n} Y)` (in the retained degrees the cohomology is
that of `Y`, in the others it is zero). -/
theorem coherent_homology_truncLE_truncGE (hiso : CoherentOfIsoInput B S hS)
    (hzero : CoherentOfIsZeroInput B S hS) (Y : DqcZ X T)
    (hY : ∀ i : ℤ, SheafOfModules.IsCoherentOnSite
      ((DerivedCategory.homologyFunctor (Modules.{u, u} B S hS X.1 X.2) i).obj Y.obj.obj))
    (n : ℤ) :
    (∀ i : ℤ, SheafOfModules.IsCoherentOnSite
      ((DerivedCategory.homologyFunctor (Modules.{u, u} B S hS X.1 X.2) i).obj
        (((standardTStructure X T).truncLE n).obj Y).obj.obj)) ∧
    (∀ i : ℤ, SheafOfModules.IsCoherentOnSite
      ((DerivedCategory.homologyFunctor (Modules.{u, u} B S hS X.1 X.2) i).obj
        (((standardTStructure X T).truncGE n).obj Y).obj.obj)) := by
  have hcoh := fun m => forall_homology_truncLE_truncGE
    (fun M : Modules.{u, u} B S hS X.1 X.2 => SheafOfModules.IsCoherentOnSite M)
    (fun e h => hiso X e h) (fun _ h => hzero X h) Y.obj.obj hY m
  refine ⟨fun i => ?_, fun i => ?_⟩
  · obtain ⟨⟨e⟩, -⟩ := nonempty_iso_truncLE_truncGE X T Y n
    exact hiso X ((DerivedCategory.homologyFunctor _ i).mapIso e).symm ((hcoh n).1 i)
  · obtain ⟨-, ⟨e⟩⟩ := nonempty_iso_truncLE_truncGE X T Y (n - 1)
    rw [sub_add_cancel] at e
    exact hiso X ((DerivedCategory.homologyFunctor _ i).mapIso e).symm ((hcoh n).2 i)

/-- **For `X` Noetherian, the standard `t`-structure restricts to `𝒯^-_c = D^-_{coh,T}(X)`**
(LP26, proof of Corollary 1.2: "The standard `t`-structure restricts to `D^-_{coh,S}(X)`"):
the standard truncations of an object of `𝒯^-_c` lie in `𝒯^-_c` (Lemma 5.9,
`lemma_5_9_minus_noetherian`, and `coherent_homology_truncLE_truncGE`). -/
theorem standardMinusC_trunc (h0AED : Tag0AEDInput B S hS)
    (h08G8 : PerfectPseudoCoherentInput B S hS) (h08FV : Tag08FVTwoInput B S hS)
    (hle : PseudoCoherentFromOfIsLEInput B S hS) (h08FU : Tag08FU2Input B S hS)
    (hpqc : PerfectQcohInput B S hS) (h08HP : Tag08HPInput B S hS) (h073B : Tag073BInput B S hS)
    (hqcs : OpenSubspaceQuasiCompactInput B S hS) (h08IK : Tag08IKInput B S hS)
    (hiso : CoherentOfIsoInput B S hS) (hzero : CoherentOfIsZeroInput B S hS)
    (hZ : B.Contains (⊤_ Scheme.{u})) (hN : IsNoetherian B S hS hZ X.1)
    (hT : IsClosed T) (hTc : _root_.IsCompact Tᶜ) (Y : DqcZ X T) (hY : standardMinusC X T Y)
    (n : ℤ) :
    standardMinusC X T (((standardTStructure X T).truncLE n).obj Y) ∧
      standardMinusC X T (((standardTStructure X T).truncGE n).obj Y) := by
  have h := lemma_5_9_minus_noetherian X h0AED h08G8 h08FV hle h08FU hpqc h08HP h073B hqcs h08IK
    hZ hN T hT hTc
  obtain ⟨hbd, hcoh⟩ := (h Y).1 hY
  obtain ⟨m, hm⟩ := (standardTStructure_minus_iff X T Y).2 hbd
  have hc := coherent_homology_truncLE_truncGE X T hiso hzero Y hcoh n
  refine ⟨(h _).2 ⟨(standardTStructure_minus_iff X T _).1 ⟨n, inferInstance⟩, hc.1⟩,
    (h _).2 ⟨(standardTStructure_minus_iff X T _).1 ⟨m, inferInstance⟩, hc.2⟩⟩

end Truncation

/-! ### The standard `t`-structure is in the preferred class -/

section Preferred

variable (X : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS) [(qcohDerived X).IsTriangulated]
  [∀ T, ObjectProperty.IsTriangulated (CohomologySupportedOn B S hS X.1 X.2 T)]
  (T : Set (points B S hS X.1))

/-- **Under standard W.A. the standard `t`-structure of `D_{qc,T}(X)` lies in the preferred
equivalence class** (LP26, proof of Lemma 5.9, `lem:characterize_T-_c`, first sentence: "Since the
standard `t`-structure appears in weak approximation data, [Neeman, Facts 1.26(i)] implies it lies
in the preferred equivalence class"). -/
theorem inPreferredClass_standardTStructure (h079Q : Tag079QInput.{u})
    (h08F3 : Tag08F3Input B S hS) (hsum : SupportedDirectSumsInput B S hS)
    (h : SatisfiesStandardWA X) (hT : IsClosed T) (hTc : _root_.IsCompact Tᶜ) :
    SumUniverse.InPreferredClass.{u} (standardTStructure X T) := by
  have : LocallySmall.{u} (DqcZ X T) := locallySmall_dqcZ h079Q _ _
  have : HasCoproducts.{u} (DqcZ X T) := hasCoproducts h08F3 hsum _ _ hT
  obtain ⟨W, hW⟩ := h T hT hTc
  exact hW ▸ inPreferredClass_of_paperData_univ W

/-- **`𝒯^-_c` may be computed for the standard `t`-structure** (LP26, proof of Lemma 5.9: "Hence,
we compute `𝒯^-_c` and `𝒯^b_c` with respect to it"): under standard W.A., for every `t`-structure
`t` of the preferred class of `D_{qc,T}(X)`, `𝒯^-_c` and `𝒯^b_c` for `t` are those for the
standard `t`-structure.  This removes the gap recorded in `Spaces/LP26/Lemma59.lean`
("Rendering"): `lemma_5_9` and its Noetherian clauses hold for every `t`-structure of the
preferred class. -/
theorem minusC_boundedC_eq_standard (h079Q : Tag079QInput.{u})
    (h08F3 : Tag08F3Input B S hS) (hsum : SupportedDirectSumsInput B S hS)
    (h : SatisfiesStandardWA X) (hT : IsClosed T) (hTc : _root_.IsCompact Tᶜ)
    (t : TStructure (DqcZ X T)) (ht : SumUniverse.InPreferredClass.{u} t) :
    minusC t (fun D => IsCompactObject.{u} D) = standardMinusC X T ∧
      boundedC t (fun D => IsCompactObject.{u} D) = standardBoundedC X T := by
  have : LocallySmall.{u} (DqcZ X T) := locallySmall_dqcZ h079Q _ _
  have : HasCoproducts.{u} (DqcZ X T) := hasCoproducts h08F3 hsum _ _ hT
  obtain ⟨W, hW⟩ := h T hT hTc
  have he : TStructureEquivalent t (standardTStructure X T) :=
    hW ▸ tStructureEquivalent_of_inPreferredClass W ht
  exact ⟨minusC_eq_of_tStructureEquivalent _ he, boundedC_eq_of_tStructureEquivalent _ he⟩

end Preferred

/-! ### Corollary 1.2, last clause -/

section Corollary

attribute [local instance] etaleModulePullback_additive preservesFiniteLimits_etaleModulePullback
  preservesFiniteColimits_etaleModulePullback

variable [∀ Y : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS, (qcohDerived Y).IsTriangulated]
  [∀ (Y : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS) T,
    ObjectProperty.IsTriangulated (CohomologySupportedOn B S hS Y.1 Y.2 T)]

/-- **Corollary 1.2** (`cor:weak_approx_spaces`), last clause, over algebraic spaces: if `X` is a
Noetherian algebraic space and `T ⊆ |X|` is closed with quasi-compact complement, then
`D_{qc,T}(X)` is **coherent** (`IsCoherent.{u}`, LP26 §2 and CHNS, Definition 10.1.1).

LP26 assumes moreover that `X` has quasi-finite separated diagonal; it is not needed
(`corollary_1_2_standard`), so the statement is stronger than the paper's.  Noetherian
(AxiomMath's `IsNoetherian`, Stacks 03EA) includes quasi-compact and quasi-separated.  Proof
(LP26's): standard W.A. (`corollary_1_2_standard`), Lemma 5.9 (`lemma_5_9_minus_noetherian`),
the restriction of the standard `t`-structure to `𝒯^-_c` (`standardMinusC_trunc`) and the
criterion of CHNS, Example 10.1.2 (`isCoherent_of_restricts`), proved here. -/
theorem corollary_1_2_coherent (h08FA : Tag08FAInput B S hS) (h08F4 : Tag08F4Input B S hS)
    (h0AFJ : Tag0AFJInput B S hS) (hpb : PullbackSupportInput B S hS)
    (hdisj : PullbackDisjointInput B S hS) (hres : EtaleRestrictionSupportInput B S hS)
    (hcounit : OpenImmersionCounitInput B S hS) (hperf : PerfectPullbackInput B S hS)
    (h08F3 : Tag08F3Input B S hS) (hsum : SupportedDirectSumsInput B S hS)
    (h0AEC : Tag0AECInput B S hS) (h0AED : Tag0AEDInput B S hS) (h079Q : Tag079QInput.{u})
    (h0A8G : Tag0A8GInput.{u}) (hRAC : RightAdjointCoproductsInput.{u})
    (hqcs : QuasiCompactSourceInput B S hS) (hcpt : CompactComplPreimageInput B S hS)
    (h08GGu : Tag08GGUnitInput B S hS) (h08GGc : Tag08GGCounitInput B S hS)
    (h073B : Tag073BInput B S hS) (h073B2 : Tag073BTwoInput B S hS)
    (h09M8 : Tag09M8Input B S hS) (hbd : PerfectBoundedAboveInput B S hS)
    (h09MB : Tag09MBInput B S hS) (h08FAb : Tag08FABoundInput B S hS)
    (hEDSc : EDSOfComplSubsetInput B S hS) (hempty : SupportEmptyInput B S hS)
    (hqcO : OpenSubspaceQuasiCompactInput B S hS) (h09IT : Tag09ITInput B S hS)
    (hqsAff : AffineQuasiSeparatedInput B S hS)
    (hex : Affine.Tag06Z0ExactInput B S hS) (hq : Affine.Tag06Z0QcohInput B S hS)
    (h06Z0 : Affine.Tag06Z0Input B S hS) (h07TY : Affine.Tag07TYInput B S hS)
    (h08G8 : PerfectPseudoCoherentInput B S hS) (h08FV : Tag08FVTwoInput B S hS)
    (hle : PseudoCoherentFromOfIsLEInput B S hS) (h08FU : Tag08FU2Input B S hS)
    (hpqc : PerfectQcohInput B S hS) (h08HP : Tag08HPInput B S hS)
    (h08IK : Tag08IKInput B S hS) (hiso : CoherentOfIsoInput B S hS)
    (hzero : CoherentOfIsZeroInput B S hS)
    (hZ : B.Contains (⊤_ Scheme.{u})) (X : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS)
    (hN : IsNoetherian B S hS hZ X.1) (T : Set (points B S hS X.1)) (hT : IsClosed T)
    (hTc : _root_.IsCompact Tᶜ) :
    IsCoherent.{u} (DqcZ X T) := by
  have hstd := corollary_1_2_standard h08FA h08F4 h0AFJ hpb hdisj hres hcounit hperf h08F3 hsum
    h0AEC h0AED h079Q h0A8G hRAC hqcs hcpt h08GGu h08GGc h073B h073B2 h09M8 hbd h09MB h08FAb hEDSc
    hempty hqcO h09IT hqsAff hex hq h06Z0 h07TY hZ X hN.1 hN.2.1
  obtain ⟨W, hW⟩ := hstd T hT hTc
  have : LocallySmall.{u} (DqcZ X T) := locallySmall_dqcZ h079Q _ _
  have : HasCoproducts.{u} (DqcZ X T) := hasCoproducts h08F3 hsum _ _ hT
  refine isCoherent_of_restricts W hW (fun Y hY => ?_) (fun Y hY n =>
    standardMinusC_trunc X T h0AED h08G8 h08FV hle h08FU hpqc h08HP h073B hqcO h08IK hiso hzero
      hZ hN hT hTc Y hY n)
  exact (standardTStructure_minus_iff X T Y).2
    (((lemma_5_9_minus_noetherian X h0AED h08G8 h08FV hle h08FU hpqc h08HP h073B hqcO h08IK hZ hN
      T hT hTc Y).1 hY).1)

end Corollary

/-! ### Non-vacuity -/

section NonVacuity

attribute [local instance] etaleModulePullback_additive preservesFiniteLimits_etaleModulePullback
  preservesFiniteColimits_etaleModulePullback

/-- **Non-vacuity of `corollary_1_2_coherent`**: over an affine, locally Noetherian base scheme
`S` (for instance `S = Spec ℤ`), the base `X = S` (`baseSpace`) is a Noetherian algebraic space
(`Statements.isNoetherianSpace_baseSpace`), `T = |S|` is closed with empty (hence compact)
complement, the two instance arguments hold (Stacks 06UQ, `SupportTriangulatedInput`), and
`D_{qc,T}(S)` is coherent (for these instances, which are `Prop`s); its preferred class is not empty: it contains the standard
`t`-structure (`inPreferredClass_standardTStructure`), so the quantifier in `IsCoherent` is not
vacuous. -/
theorem corollary_1_2_coherent_nonVacuity (h06 : Tag06UQInput B S hS)
    (hsuppT : SupportTriangulatedInput B S hS)
    (h08FA : Tag08FAInput B S hS) (h08F4 : Tag08F4Input B S hS)
    (h0AFJ : Tag0AFJInput B S hS) (hpb : PullbackSupportInput B S hS)
    (hdisj : PullbackDisjointInput B S hS) (hres : EtaleRestrictionSupportInput B S hS)
    (hcounit : OpenImmersionCounitInput B S hS) (hperf : PerfectPullbackInput B S hS)
    (h08F3 : Tag08F3Input B S hS) (hsum : SupportedDirectSumsInput B S hS)
    (h0AEC : Tag0AECInput B S hS) (h0AED : Tag0AEDInput B S hS) (h079Q : Tag079QInput.{u})
    (h0A8G : Tag0A8GInput.{u}) (hRAC : RightAdjointCoproductsInput.{u})
    (hqcs : QuasiCompactSourceInput B S hS) (hcpt : CompactComplPreimageInput B S hS)
    (h08GGu : Tag08GGUnitInput B S hS) (h08GGc : Tag08GGCounitInput B S hS)
    (h073B : Tag073BInput B S hS) (h073B2 : Tag073BTwoInput B S hS)
    (h09M8 : Tag09M8Input B S hS) (hbd : PerfectBoundedAboveInput B S hS)
    (h09MB : Tag09MBInput B S hS) (h08FAb : Tag08FABoundInput B S hS)
    (hEDSc : EDSOfComplSubsetInput B S hS) (hempty : SupportEmptyInput B S hS)
    (hqcO : OpenSubspaceQuasiCompactInput B S hS) (h09IT : Tag09ITInput B S hS)
    (hqsAff : AffineQuasiSeparatedInput B S hS)
    (hex : Affine.Tag06Z0ExactInput B S hS) (hq : Affine.Tag06Z0QcohInput B S hS)
    (h06Z0 : Affine.Tag06Z0Input B S hS) (h07TY : Affine.Tag07TYInput B S hS)
    (h08G8 : PerfectPseudoCoherentInput B S hS) (h08FV : Tag08FVTwoInput B S hS)
    (hle : PseudoCoherentFromOfIsLEInput B S hS) (h08FU : Tag08FU2Input B S hS)
    (hpqc : PerfectQcohInput B S hS) (h08HP : Tag08HPInput B S hS)
    (h08IK : Tag08IKInput B S hS) (hiso : CoherentOfIsoInput B S hS)
    (hzero : CoherentOfIsZeroInput B S hS)
    (hqsA : Statements.AffineQuasiSeparatedInput B S hS)
    (hZ : B.Contains (⊤_ Scheme.{u})) [IsAffine S] [IsLocallyNoetherian S] :
    ∃ X : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS, X = baseSpace B S hS ∧ IsNoetherian B S hS hZ X.1 ∧
      IsClosed (Set.univ : Set (points B S hS X.1)) ∧
      _root_.IsCompact (Set.univ : Set (points B S hS X.1))ᶜ ∧
      (qcohDerived X).IsTriangulated ∧
      ObjectProperty.IsTriangulated (CohomologySupportedOn B S hS X.1 X.2 Set.univ) ∧
      ∀ [(qcohDerived X).IsTriangulated]
        [ObjectProperty.IsTriangulated (CohomologySupportedOn B S hS X.1 X.2 Set.univ)],
        IsCoherent.{u} (DqcZ X Set.univ) ∧
          SumUniverse.InPreferredClass.{u} (standardTStructure X Set.univ) := by
  have : ∀ Y : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS, (qcohDerived Y).IsTriangulated :=
    fun Y => isTriangulated_qcohDerived h06 Y
  have : ∀ (Y : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS) T,
      ObjectProperty.IsTriangulated (CohomologySupportedOn B S hS Y.1 Y.2 T) :=
    fun Y => isTriangulated_support hsuppT Y
  have hN : IsNoetherian B S hS hZ (baseSpace B S hS).1 :=
    Statements.isNoetherianSpace_baseSpace B S hS hqsA hZ
  have hcl : IsClosed (Set.univ : Set (points B S hS (baseSpace B S hS).1)) := isClosed_univ
  have hco : _root_.IsCompact (Set.univ : Set (points B S hS (baseSpace B S hS).1))ᶜ := by
    rw [Set.compl_univ]
    exact isCompact_empty
  refine ⟨_, rfl, hN, hcl, hco, inferInstance, inferInstance, fun {_ _} => ⟨?_, ?_⟩⟩
  · exact corollary_1_2_coherent h08FA h08F4 h0AFJ hpb hdisj hres hcounit hperf h08F3 hsum h0AEC
      h0AED h079Q h0A8G hRAC hqcs hcpt h08GGu h08GGc h073B h073B2 h09M8 hbd h09MB h08FAb hEDSc
      hempty hqcO h09IT hqsAff hex hq h06Z0 h07TY h08G8 h08FV hle h08FU hpqc h08HP h08IK hiso
      hzero hZ (baseSpace B S hS) hN Set.univ hcl hco
  · exact inPreferredClass_standardTStructure (baseSpace B S hS) Set.univ h079Q h08F3 hsum
      (corollary_1_2_standard h08FA h08F4 h0AFJ hpb hdisj hres hcounit hperf h08F3 hsum h0AEC
        h0AED h079Q h0A8G hRAC hqcs hcpt h08GGu h08GGc h073B h073B2 h09M8 hbd h09MB h08FAb hEDSc
        hempty hqcO h09IT hqsAff hex hq h06Z0 h07TY hZ (baseSpace B S hS) hN.1 hN.2.1) hcl hco

end NonVacuity

